// Enemies (GDD v1.1 §21, App. A behaviour, App. B spawn rules, App. C shared systems): the v1.1 roster of sixteen, the Moose (note 339), the Gannet (note 340) and the
// Choir, plus two hazards (§22: track debris, formerly the Sleepers; marsh, formerly the Drift). First pass. Speeds in m/s; the GDD's Sleeper thresholds (40 / 20) are km/h, converted here.
{
  // App. A.1: every telegraph gives at least this long before a commit.
  "minReactionSeconds": 1.5,

  // Build 1121 playtest (ARCHITECTURE §8 note 263): may a creature at the controls (the Stoker's runaway, App. A.5; the Track
  // Doll's tampering, A.2) let a standing train off the brake it's held on? false: no. With steam driving (T97) a standing
  // engine off its brake pulls away, so a Stoker took a train left braked in the yard away with nobody in the cab. Under way
  // they still take it off the brake; a train at a stand stays where its driver left it.
  "tamperReleasesStandingBrake": false,

  // The damage model (the director's decision of 6 Oct 2026, GDD App. F.1; ARCHITECTURE §8 note 272): "Lethal Company
  // style. Health exists, but damage comes in a few big hits, never chip damage." Every creature's hit on a player is an
  // int field named ...Damage below, and DamageModelTests holds each to at least minHit (of player.json's 100) and the gap
  // between a creature's hits to at least minGapSeconds: a hit (35) or a heavy hit (60), so a creature on you is two or
  // three hits from death (its grab is the last, App. A.1) and a clean escape costs one. Not held to it: the train's own
  // continuous dangers (a car fire's burn, note 263's "a brush hurts, standing in it kills"; a hose's gas; a landing's
  // knock by its speed). The Stoker's door (stoker.doorBurn, then doorKill; Stoker v3, note 271) is held to minHit too.
  "damage": { "minHit": 30, "minGapSeconds": 2.5 },

  // Driven off by their rules, killed by the crew together (GDD App. F.1: "creatures mostly don't take damage; they're
  // driven off by their rules"; the director's clarification of 7 Oct 2026: "They should be driven off by rules but they
  // should also be able to be killed like in Lethal Company if the team coordinates effectively"; ARCHITECTURE §8 note 288).
  // The Grumbler, the Gaunt, the Passenger, Climbers and the Choir's ghosts (each block's drivenOff; false is the old
  // health fight): following the rule drives one off, a break that can come back; blows wear it down only while gang or
  // more different crewmates have struck it within windowSeconds (and, per creature, the setup its rule asks for). A lone
  // player's swinging never kills one. Killed, it's done for the night (a Climber or a ghost: that one), with a line in the
  // incident report naming the gang.
  "coordinatedKill": { "gang": 2, "windowSeconds": 5 },

  // Enemies farther than this from a player aren't sent to that player's machine (ARCHITECTURE §8 note 23).
  // It must cover the farthest tell anyone can hear, the hound howl's 500 m (audio/sounds/hound-howl.json);
  // AudioTests holds it to that.
  "interestRadius": 520,

  "sleepers": {
    // The director's decision, 2026-10-06 (note 265): the Sleepers go. "A derailment needs to be clearly a mistake by the
    // driver." Off, none are placed on a generated line (no Sleeper country, no "R" boards for it) and none run on any
    // line. The code stays; a mod can set this true to bring them back, with the fairer telegraph below.
    "enabled": false,
    // Telegraph: the lamp finds them at 120 m; brace (and the wet writhe you can hear) at 60 m, or, faster, as far out as
    // the train needs to brake under derailAbove: braceLeadSeconds at its speed plus a service stop (train.json
    // overspeed.brakeShare of its rated brake, plus its marginM). They derail a train only once that telegraph has been
    // up derailLeadSeconds; short of it they're the heavy damage.
    "lampRevealDistance": 120,
    "braceDistance": 60,
    "braceLeadSeconds": 4,
    "derailLeadSeconds": 4,
    "derailAbove": 11.1,
    "heavyDamageAbove": 5.6,
    "heavyDamage": 0.4,
    "minorDamage": 0.05
  },

  "cinderHounds": {
    "packSize": [3, 5],
    // In blows (App. C.2): "each takes several blows". A cannon round is four.
    "health": 3,
    "radius": 0.8,
    // Their sustainable speed: a train faster than this outruns them (App. A.3 break off).
    "maxSpeed": 19,
    // How fast they close on the train when they can.
    "closingSpeed": 3,
    "spawnBehind": 180,
    "howlSeconds": 4,
    "leapDistance": 30,
    // A hit, and a long gap (note 272; were 45 every 2.5 s): bitten twice, they're pinned (maulSeconds).
    "biteDamage": 35,
    "biteEverySeconds": 4,
    "reach": 4,
    // GDD App. F (the director, 6 Oct 2026): "Cinder Hounds that board stay aboard. They keep setting the car alight while
    // they eat the supplies, which forces the crew to confront them" (ARCHITECTURE §8 note 269). Aboard with nobody near,
    // each eats cargoPerSecond of its car's cargo, and sets the car alight (carFire below) every igniteEverySeconds it's
    // left alone. They go only dead, or with their car cut loose. stayAboard false: v1.1's drop-off after boredSeconds.
    "stayAboard": true,
    "cargoPerSecond": 0.002,
    // Note 891 (the director, 9 Oct 2026: "This is too much. Cinder Hounds should reignite every minute and a half they are
    // left aboard at the car they are currently in. Crew should have time to fight fires effectively"): 20 → 90.
    "igniteEverySeconds": 90,
    // Note 472 (the director, 8 Oct 2026: "It matters that they dont just stand there and howl, they should either patrol
    // between cars that have doors open or patrol the roofs of the cars, jumping between them if they can make the jump").
    // Aboard with nobody it can reach (note 471), a hound patrols its roof at walk m/s, and the next car's at its end: a leap
    // of leapSeconds across the coupling gap (carried across between leapFrom and leapTo of it; never onto the engine, which
    // is hooded, note 338), turning back at the ends of its ground. Its ground: the car it boarded, every car behind it, and
    // carsAhead cars ahead of it (never the car right behind the engine), so the coupling ahead of that still cuts the pack
    // loose wherever its patrol has it (note 269). Every sniffEvery s (from its own dice) it stops for sniffSeconds to sniff.
    // Over a car with a side door open, inChance of the time it drops in (dropSeconds), patrols the car inside for
    // insideSeconds, and climbs out again (climbSeconds) at an open door. Someone it can reach within chaseFrom m, it goes
    // for at chase m/s, the gaps leapt. It still eats and lights the car it's on (note 269).
    "patrol": { "on": true, "walk": 1.6, "chase": 3.5, "chaseFrom": 20, "leapSeconds": 0.9, "leapFrom": 0.25, "leapTo": 0.65,
      "sniffEvery": [8, 15], "sniffSeconds": 3, "dropSeconds": 1.0, "climbSeconds": 1.2, "inChance": 0.5, "insideSeconds": [8, 15],
      "carsAhead": 1 },
    // Note 891 (the director, 9 Oct 2026, inbox D1.2-car-fires-from-packs): "Attacking a cinder hound should reset its ignite
    // burst from its body that sets the fire. Attacking should cause it to retreat. Cinder Hounds attack the player when the
    // player is first spotted with a lunge attack by jumping at the player to bite, then retreating to do it again. Cinder
    // Hounds stop attacking and leave the train if they are pushed to the back of the train and there is a valid exit (door
    // open or roof of car)." With on: its ignite clock (igniteEverySeconds) runs the whole time it's aboard, not only alone,
    // and lights the car it's on when it runs out with nobody near (note 851's rule: never over the crew fighting the fire);
    // a blow sets it back to nought. Someone it can reach within lungeFrom m, it leaps at them over lungeSeconds (to
    // lungeShort m short of them) and bites as it lands if they're still in reach (biteDamage; down to the last, the pin),
    // backs off retreatMetres at retreatSpeed m/s, crouches crouchSeconds watching them, and comes again. A blow that
    // doesn't kill it drives it away from whoever struck it for struckSeconds at struckSpeed m/s, over the gap to the car
    // behind, and then crouches crouchSeconds before it comes again; at the back of the rear car (its roof's end, or inside
    // with one of its doors open), with leaveAtRear, it leaves the train (as the extinguisher drives it off). The spray's backing off (note 728) leaves the same way.
    // The director's answers in the inbox, 20 Oct (note 891): "Every 90 seconds and there needs to be an associated animation
    // of how that happens": its clock run out, it stops and winds up igniteWindUpSeconds (its cracks blazing up, embers
    // rising off it), and the burst from its body lights the car at the end of it; someone coming near, or a blow, and it
    // breaks off. And the hounds that ride longer should "flee": the fleeAfterBlows-th blow on it aboard (0: never), it gives
    // up and jumps off the train wherever it is.
    // on false: note 472's bite every biteEverySeconds where it stands, the clock only while it's alone, no wind-up.
    "aboard": { "on": true, "lungeFrom": 4, "lungeSeconds": 0.5, "lungeShort": 0.8, "retreatMetres": 3, "retreatSpeed": 2.5,
      "crouchSeconds": 2, "struckSeconds": 1, "struckSpeed": 3.5, "leaveAtRear": true, "igniteWindUpSeconds": 2,
      "fleeAfterBlows": 2 },
    // A trial (note 915, #612's answer to note 863's pack fires: one pack left alone aboard lit 26 in a night): on, once a
    // pack's hounds have lit `fires` fires between them, each leaves the train as it would bored (not driven off), lighting
    // nothing more. Off until measured.
    "sated": { "on": false, "fires": 3 },
    "boredSeconds": 6,
    // App. B.3: needs sustained speed first.
    "minTrainSpeed": 8,
    // GDD v1.1 App. A.3 break off: "rear cannon hit". A round from a gun in range of the pack inside this window, and a
    // running hound peels away (the v1.0 "sustained fire" was nine; a cannon that reloads by hand fires one).
    "suppressRounds": 1,
    "suppressWindowSeconds": 4,
    // App. A.1 GRAB: a crewmate bitten down to their last is pinned; friends have this long to club it off.
    "maulSeconds": 8
  },

  // App. C.1 GRAB, shared by every enemy that holds someone: a friend pulls a victim free with Use this close (where the
  // enemy allows it) or hits the holder. Alone (a crew of one), holding Use for soloStruggle seconds is a try at breaking
  // the hold (ARCHITECTURE §8 note 92): one try a grab, and it works soloStruggleChance of the time (the director, 13 Oct
  // 2026, App. C.1: "holding e shouldn't always result in escape it should at best give me a 15% chance of escape"; note
  // 681). Then raised to a coin flip (the director's playtest, 14 Oct: "hold the struggle when playing solo really should
  // have a higher rate of success. Damn, yeah, run lost"; note 737): 0.15 to 0.5. soloStruggle is shorter than every
  // creature's hold (the Householder's grabSeconds, 6, the shortest), so the try comes before the kill.
  // In a crew, a held player with no living crewmate within crewStruggleBeyond m (proximity voice's reach: nobody near enough
  // to hear and come) can struggle the same way, at crewStruggleChance: lower than alone's, since a friend may still come
  // (the audit's R3, the director, 14 Oct: "Approved for Grabbed"; note 756). crewStruggleBeyond 0: alone only, as before.
  "grab": { "pullReach": 1.6, "soloStruggleOn": true, "soloStruggle": 4, "soloStruggleChance": 0.5, "crewStruggleBeyond": 26,
    "crewStruggleChance": 0.2 },

  // App. C.2 melee with train tools: the shovel, the crowbar and the wrench (GDD §12, §1322) swing; enemy health below is in
  // blows of the crowbar, the tool everyone starts with (player.json kit). App. C.2: "the boiler player's shovel doubling as
  // the crew's best club is intended tension": it's the shovel's blow that's the best (note 275), and there's the one, by the
  // firebox (boiler.json shovelInHand). The wrench in the cab is short in the haft, "nothing but a wrench" (§13). T108: with
  // nothing in hand, a fist does barehanded of a blow. DESIGN-TODO: the GDD gives no numbers; these are a first pass that
  // keeps every creature's health a whole number of crowbar blows and takes a 3-health one in two of the shovel's.
  "melee": { "reach": 2.2, "coneDegrees": 70, "swingSeconds": 0.8, "shovel": 1.5, "crowbar": 1, "wrench": 0.75, "barehanded": 0.25 },

  // Every creature's body as a cannonball finds it (GDD App. F.1, build 1121: "the guns do nothing. Rounds don't collide
  // where they land and have no visible effect on the monsters"; ARCHITECTURE §8 note 290). A stack of spheres, each
  // [radius, height of its centre over where the creature stands] in m, fitted to its model as drawn (content/art/models:
  // the Ribbit at its 1.4 scale; a long, low body, the Whistler's, the Climber's, a hound's, by one sphere round its
  // middle). The body stands while the creature is in the open (Enemy.Exposed: by default wherever a tool's blow can land
  // on it), and a ball that finds it lands on it as a blow of combat.json guns.damagePerRound by the gunner, answered by
  // the creature's own rule for a blow. No body (a ball goes through): the Fire Flies (a swarm) and the Choir's ghosts.
  // A sleeping Gaunt is curled to gauntAsleep of its height.
  "bodies": {
    "cinderHound": [[0.75, 0.4]],
    "climber": [[0.65, 0.3]],
    "trackDoll": [[0.55, 0.7], [0.4, 1.6]],
    "ribbit": [[0.6, 0.55]],
    "gaunt": [[0.5, 0.6], [0.5, 1.5], [0.45, 2.4], [0.35, 3.1]],
    "grumbler": [[0.55, 0.55], [0.55, 1.3], [0.35, 1.8]],
    "whistler": [[0.6, 0.3]],
    "dragger": [[0.45, 0]],
    "follower": [[0.3, 0.05]],
    "sootChildren": [[0.35, 0.4], [0.3, 0.9]],
    "carHugger": [[1.3, 0.6], [1.2, 1.9]],
    "passenger": [[0.4, 0.5], [0.4, 1.15], [0.3, 1.6]],
    "stoker": [[0.45, 0.45], [0.4, 1.1]],
    "tippyToesie": [[0.4, 0.6], [0.4, 1.4], [0.3, 2.0]],
    // The barrel and the hump (note 339); its rack stops nothing, a round in it is a miss.
    "moose": [[0.9, 1.6], [0.9, 2.1], [0.6, 2.6]],
    // Its breast and sacs, and the head over them (note 340): standing on a roof 2.3 m tall; in the air, about where it flies.
    "gannet": [[1.0, 0.7], [0.6, 1.6]],
    // Child-high, hunched over (note 362).
    "mourners": [[0.35, 0.45], [0.3, 0.9]],
    // Knee-high, a crate over its head when it carries (note 592).
    "pickers": [[0.3, 0.3]],
    // A dog-sized rat, low to the ground (note 790).
    "mouseMoose": [[0.35, 0.3]],
    // The house creatures (notes 583–586): the Lodger and the Householder man-sized; the Hanger's sac, up in the roof.
    "lodger": [[0.35, 0.5], [0.3, 1.2]],
    "householder": [[0.35, 0.5], [0.3, 1.3]],
    "hanger": [[0.45, 0]],
    // A bear-sized beaver, its shoulders over its head (note 363).
    "towerJaw": [[0.8, 0.7], [0.6, 1.3]],
    // Its plated back, a handcart's bulk (note 366).
    "freightBeetle": [[0.75, 0.7], [0.6, 0.7]],
    // A stooped man (note 364); Hotbox half out of its truck, low (note 367).
    "brakeman": [[0.4, 0.5], [0.4, 1.1], [0.3, 1.55]],
    "hotbox": [[0.45, 0.2]],
    // Its body across the gap, low (note 365).
    "knotter": [[0.35, 0]],
    // The Waker stood, 62 m (note 940): his legs, his hips and belly, his chest and his head; on his knees, kneelStoop of it.
    "waker": [[7, 8], [7, 20], [8, 32], [8, 42], [6, 52]]
  },
  "gauntAsleep": 0.35,

  // TRACK DOLL · sight · forward (App. A.2, B.2). Revealed in the lamp at lampRevealDistance, or in the dark only this close.
  // Stopped (below stoppedBelow m/s) short of it: gone for the run. Hit: it haunts. Cornered (players within cornerWithin at
  // both ends of its car) it can be clubbed; approached from one side it vanishes when anyone's within vanishNear and moves
  // car every hauntMoveSeconds. Past stage 1 (below), an empty cab for tamperAfterEmpty s and it's at the controls. A toy within toyReach: it
  // takes it and leaves. DESIGN-TODO: how much cargo "admiring" costs is unstated; cargoPerSecond is a guess.
  "trackDoll": {
    "lampRevealDistance": 200, "darkRevealDistance": 25, "spawnAhead": 700, "stoppedBelow": 0.3, "health": 2,
    "hauntMoveSeconds": 25, "vanishNear": 3, "cornerWithin": 6, "tamperAfterEmpty": 8, "toyReach": 1.8,
    "cargoPerSecond": 0.001,
    // B.2: needs a straight this long ahead (so the lamp can find it), and weighs this much more with the cab empty.
    "straightNeeded": 250, "emptyCabWeight": 2,
    // T121 playtest ("I shot the track doll and it did nothing while she was on the track"): a forward cannon's ball that
    // hits her on the rail shatters her, gone for the run, the same outcome as stopping short (App. A.2's VANISH), so the
    // train no longer strikes her. The GDD gives the brakes as the answer and doesn't say a cannon isn't one; it's loud and
    // costs the reload, which keeps it a cost. Her body on the rail is in bodies, above (a large porcelain doll; note 290).
    // cannonShatters off: the ball goes through her (ARCHITECTURE §8 note 171).
    "cannonShatters": true,
    // The director's decision of 6 Oct 2026 (GDD App. F.1, "The Track Doll escalates if ignored"; ARCHITECTURE §8 note
    // 268): aboard, she's no problem at first and gets worse only for being left alone. Her neglect clock runs a second a
    // second while no living crewmate is in her car or within attendRadius m of her, and attended it winds back at
    // attendedEase a second. Stage 1 (from the strike): she haunts the cars, admires the cargo and giggles; she never goes
    // to the cab. Stage 2 at controlsAfter s of neglect: an empty cab (tamperAfterEmpty) and she's at the controls, but
    // only nudging the regulator up to nudgeThrottle on one beat in three; she never touches the brake. Stage 3 at
    // releaseAfter s: the full tampering (the regulator open, the brake on and off), and once she's been at the controls
    // releaseAfterAtControls s at that stage on a visit, a standing train's held brake too (finalStageReleasesBrake; the
    // one exception to tamperReleasesStandingBrake above). A haunting doll is never dismissed for want of company (the
    // director's lingerSeconds). Each stage is telegraphed warnSeconds before it comes (she's restless: replicated,
    // her giggle quickens, and at stage 2 she rattles the brake handle without moving it). Getting her off the train (a
    // toy, or cornered and clubbed) ends it; a new doll starts at stage 1.
    "controlsAfter": 120, "releaseAfter": 300, "warnSeconds": 30, "attendRadius": 8, "attendedEase": 0.5,
    "nudgeThrottle": 0.25, "releaseAfterAtControls": 12, "finalStageReleasesBrake": true
  },

  // CAR HUGGER · vibration · rear (App. A.3, B.3). Latched: the train's top speed capped at speedCap m/s (the train drags
  // dragFactor times harder above it), the rear car's shell and loot eaten at these rates; eaten through, the car drops.
  // Anyone in front of its mouth (mouthReach) is swallowed: swallowSeconds for friends to pull them free. It heals
  // regenPerSecond blows a second, so one player can barely out-hit it. Lurks at a marsh or bridge lurkAheadMin-Max ahead
  // on a grade under maxGrade %. B.3: weighs lowSpeedWeight more with the train under lowSpeed m/s. Every breachEaten of
  // the shell it eats (25 s at shellPerSecond: past the guard van's platform, into the end wall, as the art eats it) it's
  // through the end wall: the car's breached (spec B.9, train.json breach), and boarded up it's through again 25 s on.
  "carHugger": {
    "speedCap": 9, "dragFactor": 1.6, "shellPerSecond": 0.004, "lootPerSecond": 0.006, "mouthReach": 1.6,
    "swallowSeconds": 10, "health": 16, "regenPerSecond": 0.15, "lurkAheadMin": 250, "lurkAheadMax": 800, "maxGrade": 0.6,
    "lowSpeed": 8, "lowSpeedWeight": 2, "minCars": 2, "breachEaten": 0.1,
    // A trial (note 915, #612; "test creature spawn first"): App. B.3's "low ground", never laid (note 875: its spot held 1.4%
    // of an ordinary night, under 0.1% on frontier:7). On, the line plan's main-line stretches of these biomes are spots
    // too (the first level point every step m), and lurkAheadMax replaces the block's own. Off until measured and confirmed.
    // Note 970 (the director, 21 Oct 2026: "We need more situations the Hugger can pop up, not just marshes"), behind the same
    // switch: tags, the line plan's director tags on the main line that are spots too (a cutting's wet floor, a culvert's
    // water crossing, low ground, the woods' edge, a blind curve's exit), searched like the biomes; stood, the far side of a
    // train stood under `below` m/s, at its rear car, with no living crewmate within unseenM of it.
    "lowGround": { "on": false, "biomes": ["marsh", "dykeland", "contaminatedMarsh"], "lurkAheadMax": 1500, "step": 50,
      "tags": ["low_ground", "water_crossing", "cutting", "dark_forest", "blind_curve_exit"],
      "stood": { "on": true, "below": 0.5, "unseenM": 20 } }
  },

  // WHISTLER · absence · flank (App. A.4, B.4). Boards at a stop; whistleAfterStop s into the next stop it blows the
  // whistle for whistleSeconds (it feeds the loudness meter). A player passing within passReach of its gap with nobody
  // else within pairRadius is snatched and carried off at runSpeed to a nest nestDistance m out, eaten nestSeconds after.
  // Two players within spotReach of the gap and it flees. B.4: stopWeight: it's weighted toward routes with stops.
  // T128 (build 1121: "a creature carried the director up a mountainside"; ARCHITECTURE §8 note 273): the nest is straight
  // out from the gap across the line, on the side they were taken from if it can be, at nestDistance (60 → 30: inside
  // train.json recovery.corridorM, Line Plan §12.6's walkable corridor; it went 60 m out in a straight line at rail height,
  // and wherever the land rose the player was stood up on the hillside when it let go), shorter by nestStep down to
  // nestMinDistance where the land won't have it. Its run there is over the ground, and the way has to be land a person can
  // run: no 2 m of it steeper than nestMaxSlope (rise over run), never more than nestMaxRise m above or below the rail, no
  // water. Neither side has any: the formation's edge. At a generated stop it runs to the nest the layout put out on the
  // stop's emptiest side (level-design H.2; note 314), the nearest within nestSiteReach of its gap that the same rules allow
  // and whose way there misses every building. Nowhere does its run go through a wall.
  "whistler": {
    "stoppedBelow": 0.3, "whistleAfterStop": 4, "whistleSeconds": 2.5, "passReach": 1.6, "pairRadius": 3, "spotReach": 2.5,
    "runSpeed": 4.5, "nestDistance": 30, "nestMinDistance": 8, "nestStep": 4, "nestMaxSlope": 0.4, "nestMaxRise": 6, "nestSiteReach": 110,
    "nestSeconds": 20, "health": 3, "stopWeight": 0.3, "minCars": 2
  },

  // The world is solid (the director, 6 Oct 2026: "creatures, carries and players must respect the terrain and geometry";
  // ARCHITECTURE §8 note 279). Once the creatures have stepped, what's loose in the world is held out of the stops' and the
  // fortresses' buildings and inside a tunnel's lining, by the widest sphere of its body (bodies, above). By kind: "ground"
  // walks on the land (a Ribbit's hop, a Gaunt walking up after its waker, a feral Grumbler), but within climbM of a car it
  // may be up its side; "air" flies, never lower than airClearM over the land (the Choir); "none" goes its own way (the
  // Whistler's run is laid clear of walls, above, a Follower crawls along the cars, the Soot Children answer a voice).
  "solidity": {
    "climbM": 2.5, "airClearM": 0.2,
    "kinds": { "ribbit": "ground", "gaunt": "ground", "grumbler": "ground", "choir": "air", "whistler": "none", "follower": "none", "sootChildren": "none",
      "mourners": "ground", "freightBeetle": "ground", "towerJaw": "ground", "pickers": "ground",
      "mouseMoose": "ground" }
  },

  // TIPPY TOESIE · absence · interior (App. A.5, B.5). Picks a player idle (moving under idleBelow m/s) for idleSeconds with
  // nobody within aloneRadius; starts startBehind m behind them and creeps at approachSpeed (slower at a crew of two).
  // Looked at (within seenDegrees of their view) it flees, up to maxFlees times, and waits waitAfterSeen s. At reach it
  // covers their mouth: suffocateSeconds for a friend to break it.
  "tippyToesie": {
    "idleSeconds": 5, "idleBelow": 0.3, "aloneRadius": 8, "startBehind": 9, "approachSpeed": 0.6, "approachSpeedCrewOfTwo": 0.4,
    "seenDegrees": 50, "reach": 0.8, "suffocateSeconds": 20, "waitAfterSeen": 20, "maxFlees": 3, "health": 2, "minCrew": 2,
    "perIdleWeight": 1,
    // Boarding-first (GDD App. F.1, note 286): "nothing acts inside the train unless it boarded". It slips aboard only with
    // the train under boardBelow (m/s: a stop), and stays hidden aboard after it until it's fled maxFlees times. Shut doors
    // don't stop it: it opens them without a sound.
    "boardBelow": 0.3
  },

  // FIRE FLIES · light · interior (App. A.5, B.5). On a lit car lamp in a dark section; left igniteSeconds, the car
  // catches (carFire below). Break off: the lamp out, or the train over pullAwaySpeed m/s for pullAwaySeconds.
  // GDD App. F (the director, 6 Oct 2026): "Car lamps start lit. Their pull on Fire Flies is rare, and only while the car
  // is stopped." The director sends them only while the train's under stoppedBelow m/s, at stoppedWeight of their B.5
  // weight; and A.5's "pulls away at speed" is getting under way: pullAwaySpeed was 15 (ARCHITECTURE §8 note 269).
  "fireFlies": {
    "igniteSeconds": 20, "pullAwaySpeed": 2, "pullAwaySeconds": 8, "depthWeight": 2, "stoppedBelow": 0.3, "stoppedWeight": 0.5,
    // Boarding-first (GDD App. F.1, note 286): "shut doors stop some boarders". A lit car with every door and its hatch shut
    // (and no breach) keeps them off its lamp: at a stop, it's the cars left open with their lamps lit that draw them.
    "shutCarKeepsOut": true
  },

  // WHERE THE OUTSIDE CREATURES START (level-design H.2; GDD B.6; ARCHITECTURE §8 note 309). A generated stop's layout says
  // where each lives; the director still says when. At the stops within `around` m of the train: Ribbits come out of the
  // warren nearest the ground crew within `warrenReach` (a stop whose warrens are all further has none to send); the Gaunt
  // sleeps in its roost if it's within `roostReach`; a child calls from its call within `callReach`; a Follower takes only a
  // crewmate standing in one of its grounds (its radius and `groundMargin`). Nothing comes out closer than `minOut` m. A
  // hand-laid route's stops have no layouts: there they come from out in the dark round the ground crew, as before.
  "sites": { "around": 300, "minOut": 12, "warrenReach": 70, "roostReach": 400, "callReach": 160, "groundMargin": 4 },

  // RIBBITS · sight · outside (App. A.6, B.6). A pack of packSize (never more than the crew) hops at hopSpeed toward the
  // nearest group smaller than it (players within groupRadius of each other: App. C.6); in tongueReach it freezes one and
  // eats for devourSeconds. They lose interest past giveUpBeyond m.
  // Note 558 (the director, 9 Oct: "they overlapped each other a lot"): the leader comes straight in, the rest fan out
  // either side of it, fan degrees a place apart round the catch, ringOut m from them (the leader to the hop's own 0.8);
  // within the last fanFrom m of the catch they make for those places; and none comes nearer a packmate than spacing m.
  // Past a right angle, so with the catch down on their back (laid away from the leader) the others are at their sides.
  "ribbits": {
    // minCrew (note 795, was 2): a crew of one meets a lone Ribbit (the pack is never more than the crew); it can struggle
    // free of the tongue (grab.soloStruggleChance).
    "packSize": [2, 4], "minCrew": 1, "hopSpeed": 4, "groupRadius": 8, "tongueReach": 4, "devourSeconds": 8, "giveUpBeyond": 45,
    "spawnOut": 35, "health": 2, "perGroundWeight": 0.5, "fan": 100, "ringOut": 1.05, "fanFrom": 10, "spacing": 1.15
  },

  // GRUMBLER · sound · corrupted human (App. A.8, B.8). Gnaws the food crates at a facility; hit, it hunts the last to hit
  // it at huntSpeed. It regenerates regenPerSecond blows a second unless two players have hit it within gangSeconds.
  // Aboard with a crate, it eats cargoPerSecond. B.8: foodWeight more with food aboard.
  // Note 272 (App. F.1, no chip damage): a hit every 3 s (were 15 every 1.5 s), and it mauls once it's bitten you twice
  // (grabBelowHealth was 30).
  // Note 288 (drivenOff; "gang up or leave it alone"): feral, with gangOf (coordinatedKill.gang) of the crew within
  // gangRadius m of it and no gang striking it, it breaks off after outnumberedSeconds (letting go of a maul) and scuttles
  // off for fleeSeconds, then back to gnawing, calmed. Only the gang's blows take its health (and it fights them).
  "grumbler": {
    "health": 6, "regenPerSecond": 1.5, "gangSeconds": 5, "huntSpeed": 3.5, "reach": 1.4, "biteDamage": 35, "biteEvery": 3,
    "grabBelowHealth": 35, "maulSeconds": 8, "cargoPerSecond": 0.004, "foodWeight": 2,
    "drivenOff": true, "gangRadius": 3, "outnumberedSeconds": 2, "fleeSeconds": 8
  },

  // THE CHOIR's swarm (App. A.7): ghosts come when the meter's gathered (combat.json "choir"). Each seizes anyone outside
  // or behind no shut door for seizeSeconds (broken only by killing it); hit, it hits back. It flies flySpeed m/s faster
  // than the train. Quiet for disperseQuietSeconds and they go. Note 272 (App. F.1, no chip damage): a ghost's hit back is a
  // hit, at most once every hitBackEvery s however fast it's struck (was 15 for every blow).
  // Note 288 (drivenOff; "hush, and shut every door"): a seize breaks when the meter's under its threshold for
  // hushBreakSeconds (the ghost goes) or its catch is behind a shut door (it goes back to the doors); blows don't break it.
  // Only the gang's blows with the crew holding quiet take a ghost's health; the last of the swarm killed, it's spent.
  "choir": {
    "ghosts": 4, "health": 6, "seizeSeconds": 12, "flySpeed": 6, "hitBackDamage": 35, "hitBackEvery": 3, "disperseQuietSeconds": 10,
    "around": 12, "drivenOff": true, "hushBreakSeconds": 3
  },

  // THE MOOSE · movement (trespass), sound · outside (GDD §21, App. A.6, B.6; the director's decisions of 7 Oct 2026;
  // ARCHITECTURE §8 note 339; docs/design/creatures/moose.md). A hyper-aggressive, territorial moose, too big to get on the
  // train. Grazing beside a stop, its aggro (0-100) rises crowdPerSecond with anyone on the ground within crowdAt m
  // (closePerSecond within closeAt), voicePerSecond at full voice (by the Voice byte, over talkingAbove of 255) with anyone
  // talking within hearVoice m, and by trainPass once as a train goes by within trainPassAt m; a hit fills it. It falls
  // calmPerSecond with nobody crowding or talking. listenAt (head up, ears turning) and warnAt (ears flat, the sac ridge up)
  // are its tells. Full, its target is whoever put the most in (whoever hits it, from then on). In sight (sightRange, no
  // building or car between) it closes at huntSpeed, squares up squareUpSeconds within squareUpAt[1] m (its heading locks
  // at the end) and charges at chargeSpeed, overrunning overrun m, then wheels round in wheelSeconds. Its body is rackSpan
  // across: nothing narrower lets it in. A building in the way snags it snagSeconds; a car or the track's clearance pulls it
  // up; blockedCharges of those without reaching its target and it gives up. A charge through anyone on the ground (within
  // hitReach of its rack) is a hit of chargeDamage; on someone at or under grabBelowHealth it pins them for pinSeconds, and
  // a blow from anyone else takes it off them (they're its target then). Out of sight it searches at searchSpeed where it
  // lost them, searchSeconds; a voice within hearVoice gives anyone away. Lost within lostAtCar m of a car they're aboard,
  // it rams the car every ramEvery s for ramSeconds (a ram is only a sound and a shudder). It gives up past leashRadius from
  // its ground, and when the train pulls away. It can't be killed. Never within trackClearance m of a track's centre
  // (movingClearance while the train moves): it's never on the rail. Gone past goneBeyond m from the train.
  // Spawns (B.6): at a stop, groundAt m out from the consist's middle; every tier, tierWeights by tier; biomeWeights by the
  // line's biome (1 unlisted); perGroundWeight more per player on the ground; minCrew (1: a lone player struggles free, the
  // solo rule, as from every grab). Beside the line on the run, lineside per 10 km by tier (times the biome's weight),
  // linesideAhead m ahead and linesideOut m out: the line's own, not the director's.
  "moose": {
    "crowdAt": 20, "crowdPerSecond": 25, "closeAt": 12, "closePerSecond": 70,
    "hearVoice": 15, "talkingAbove": 40, "voicePerSecond": 40,
    "trainPassAt": 25, "trainPass": 25, "calmPerSecond": 15,
    // The band (note 711; the director, 14 Oct: "stopping the moose"): a crewmate playing within bandHears m stops it to
    // listen, whatever it was doing short of a pin: it forgets its target, stands with its head to the music, and its temper
    // falls bandCalmPerSecond (0 bandHears: it doesn't care).
    "bandHears": 30, "bandCalmPerSecond": 30,
    "listenAt": 20, "warnAt": 50,
    "squareUpAt": [12, 30], "squareUpSeconds": 2.5, "huntSpeed": 4.5,
    "chargeSpeed": 11, "overrun": 8, "wheelSeconds": 2.5, "rackSpan": 3.2, "hitReach": 0.5, "snagSeconds": 4, "blockedCharges": 3,
    "chargeDamage": 60, "grabBelowHealth": 40, "pinSeconds": 12,
    "sightRange": 60, "searchSpeed": 2.5, "searchSeconds": 25, "leashRadius": 80,
    "lostAtCar": 5, "ramEvery": 3, "ramSeconds": 15,
    "trackClearance": 3.2, "movingClearance": 6, "goneBeyond": 600,
    "groundAt": [30, 60], "minCrew": 1, "perGroundWeight": 0.5,
    "tierWeights": { "local": 1, "frontier": 1.5, "deadLines": 2, "deepTerritory": 2.5 },
    "lineside": { "local": 2, "frontier": 3, "deadLines": 4, "deepTerritory": 5 },
    "linesideOut": [8, 22], "linesideAhead": 300,
    "biomeWeights": { "marsh": 2, "plains": 1.5, "contaminatedMarsh": 1.5, "coast": 0.5, "blackForest": 1, "forestEdge": 1, "mountain": 1,
      "deadTown": 0.5, "industrialRuin": 0.3, "slag": 0.3 }
  },

  // THE GANNET · sight · flank (GDD §21, App. A.4, B.4; the director's decisions of 7 Oct 2026; ARCHITECTURE §8 note 340;
  // docs/design/creatures/gannet.md; the orchestrator's S3). One enormous corrupted seabird that rides a fast train: the
  // train over arriveAbove m/s for arriveSeconds, out of a tunnel, and it comes, soaring soarRadius m round a car soarHeight
  // m up at flySpeed. Someone walking a roof (over preyAbove m/s on it, not seated) is its prey: it hangs over them
  // hangSeconds, then folds: its line locks on where they'll be foldSeconds on, and it strikes there at the end. Within
  // strikeRadius of the strike, a stab of stabDamage (it can't kill) and up again; nobody there, on the roof: stuck
  // stuckSeconds (a blow lands only now, or in a pin). A pass every diveEvery s. Whoever hits it (a blow, a ball) is its
  // mark: when it's next due, it banks round bankSeconds (the telegraph: inside a car or the cab is shelter) and comes down
  // on them, on a roof or on the ground within markReach, and pecks pecks times, peckEvery s apart, the last their death;
  // driveOffBlows blows from friends in the pin drive it off (the last of them its mark). health in blows; under
  // giveUpBelow it leaves for the run; killed, its head is a trophy (loot.json trophies.gannet). Under stallBelow for
  // stallSeconds, in a tunnel, or quietSeconds with nobody walking the roofs and its mark inside, it peels off, back after
  // returnSeconds once the train's run fast again. Spawns (B.4): every tier, tierWeights; biomeWeights by the line's biome
  // (1 unlisted); perRoofWeight more per player on the roofs; minCars. Once a run (it comes back on its own).
  "gannet": {
    "arriveAbove": 18, "arriveSeconds": 30, "stallBelow": 12, "stallSeconds": 6, "quietSeconds": 60, "returnSeconds": 180,
    "soarHeight": [20, 35], "soarRadius": 14, "flySpeed": 12,
    "preyAbove": 0.8, "hangSeconds": 2, "foldSeconds": 1.6, "diveEvery": [8, 12],
    "strikeRadius": 0.9, "stabDamage": 35, "stuckSeconds": 4,
    "bankSeconds": 2.5, "pecks": 4, "peckEvery": 3, "driveOffBlows": 3,
    "health": 12, "giveUpBelow": 4, "markReach": 200, "minCars": 2, "perRoofWeight": 1,
    // A trial (note 915, #612; the director, 20 Oct 2026, to note 875's question 1: "13"): on, it comes over the train at
    // lowArrive.arriveAbove (no ordinary night reached B.13's 18 m/s; at 13 its 30 s held on every one) and peels off under
    // lowArrive.stallBelow. "Test creature spawn first": off until measured and confirmed; spec B.13 follows then.
    "lowArrive": { "on": false, "arriveAbove": 13, "stallBelow": 10 },
    "tierWeights": { "local": 1, "frontier": 1.5, "deadLines": 2, "deepTerritory": 2.5 },
    "biomeWeights": { "coast": 3, "dykeland": 3, "plains": 1.5, "marsh": 1.5, "contaminatedMarsh": 1.5, "blackForest": 0.3,
      "forestEdge": 0.5, "mountain": 1, "deadTown": 1.5 },
    // Gerald and the garden gnomes (note 715; train.json composition.whimsy): of its passes with one aboard, this share it
    // dives on one of them instead (hangs over it, folds, and carries it off), whoever's walking.
    "decoyPull": 0.25
  },

  // THE MOURNERS · absence · outside (GDD §21, App. A.6, B.6; the director's brief of 8 Oct 2026; ARCHITECTURE §8 note 362;
  // docs/design/creatures/mourners.md). Small ash-pale scavengers that come only after a crewmate dies: a body lying off
  // the train (not carried, not in a car the engine pulls) for "after" s brings a group, "count" of them by tier, arriveAt m
  // off it on the side away from the line, edging in over comeSeconds and waiting waitAt m off. They never touch the
  // living. Anyone within shy m of one starts it back to startleTo m off them (at scatter m/s), and it edges in again after
  // returnAfter s. Nobody within shy m of the body, the two nearest it creep in (creep m/s; from far off they come at approach m/s) and take it (within takeReach):
  // one hauls it straight away from the nearest track at drag m/s, held holdAt m in front of it holdHeight m up, the other
  // beside. A crewmate within dropWithin m of the body, or a blow on any of them, and it's dropped; a blow kills one (health
  // in blows) and the rest scatter for scatterOnDeath s. A body carried is followed, never touched; one brought home (in a
  // car the engine pulls) sends them off; one hauled lostAt m from the track is gone (its refund and its kit), and they go.
  // Leaving, they're gone once well off or after leaveSeconds. Not the director's: they cost it nothing and come for every
  // body ("enabled" off: never).
  "mourners": {
    "enabled": true, "after": 15,
    "count": { "local": 3, "frontier": 4, "deadLines": 5, "deepTerritory": 6 },
    "arriveAt": 40, "comeSeconds": 6, "waitAt": 10, "shy": 6, "startleTo": 12, "dropWithin": 3, "takeReach": 0.9,
    "creep": 1.4, "approach": 3, "drag": 1.6, "scatter": 4, "holdAt": 0.7, "holdHeight": 0.5,
    "returnAfter": 4, "scatterOnDeath": 6, "lostAt": 120, "leaveSeconds": 30, "health": 1
  },

  // THE PICKERS · sight · outside (GDD §21, App. A.6, B.6; the director's pick to prototype, 9 Oct 2026; ARCHITECTURE §8
  // note 592; docs/design/creatures/pickers.md). Knee-high scavengers in a yard's drains. "after" s once the train stands at a
  // facility with loose crates within facilityReach m, a group comes up out of the drains at the foot of the yard's sheds (up
  // to "drains" of them, drainOff m out from a shed's wall on the track's side), "count" by tier and perTwoCrew more for
  // every two of the crew past two, one drain to each in turn, each a moment coming up (emergeSeconds). Each runs (run m/s) for
  // the nearest loose crate on the ground nobody's guarding (a living crewmate within guardWithin m) and no other Picker has (a
  // heavy crate takes two), takes it up (within takeReach) over its head (holdHeight m up) and carries it to its drain (carry
  // m/s; a heavy crate carryHeavy m/s, with a second heaveBeside m beside), and down it goes with it within atDrain m: the
  // crate's gone, and it comes up again downSeconds later. Unladen, anyone within shyWithin m sends it back down its drain for
  // shySeconds (stood over its drain, you keep it down). Laden, a crewmate within
  // biteWithin m is bitten (bite, never a kill; once in biteEvery s) and it drops the crate and scatters. A blow kills one
  // (health in blows), and every one within scatterWithin m drops what it has and runs to its drain for scatterSeconds. The
  // train gone from the stop (not shunting at it), they all go down their drains
  // (gone after leaveSeconds, whether or not they got there). Not the director's: they cost it nothing, and come to
  // every yard stop with loose crates ("enabled" off: never).
  "pickers": {
    "enabled": true, "after": 20,
    "count": { "local": 3, "frontier": 4, "deadLines": 6, "deepTerritory": 8 }, "perTwoCrew": 1,
    "facilityReach": 80, "drains": 3, "drainOff": 1.2, "emergeSeconds": 0.8, "downSeconds": 3,
    "guardWithin": 4, "shyWithin": 3, "shySeconds": 4, "run": 4.8, "carry": 2.6, "carryHeavy": 1.6, "takeReach": 0.9, "holdHeight": 1.0,
    "heaveBeside": 0.9, "atDrain": 1.0, "biteWithin": 1.2, "bite": 8, "biteEvery": 2,
    "scatterWithin": 10, "scatterSeconds": 6, "leaveSeconds": 12, "health": 1
  },

  // THE MOUSE MOOSE · sight · outside (GDD §21; the director, 15 Oct 2026: "a creature that wanders yards stealing loot. It
  // does so very slowly, and once it gets out of position so that the crane can't reach it, then you can't get it as a
  // player"; ARCHITECTURE §8 note 790; docs/design/creatures/mouse-moose.md). A mutant rat with little moose antlers. It comes
  // out of its hole (holeOut m out past a casting, away from the track) and creeps in (creep m/s) to one of the castings a
  // crane at the stop still has to load, gets its teeth in it on the hole's side (stood grip m off its face, its snout's
  // length) for biteSeconds (the reaction window), and drags it back toward its hole at drag m/s: very slowly. Once the hook
  // can no longer be put within the crane's rigReach of it (asked every reachEvery ticks), the casting is taken: nobody can
  // load it, and it's dragged on
  // at dragAway m/s; at its hole (within atHole m) it's gone. A living crewmate within scareWithin m (as the crow flies: the
  // crane's operator up in the cab is no guard), or a blow, and it lets go and bolts for its hole (run m/s), hides there
  // hideSeconds and comes back for the same casting; the scaresToGiveUp-th scare off one, and it goes for another (the nearest
  // it can take). It never hurts anyone, and nothing kills it. It goes when the train's more than leaveBeyond m from its
  // crane, or there's nothing left to take. Spawns: stopped at a facility whose crane (its own or a yard's) has a casting
  // stacked; every tier, tierWeights; one at a stop.
  "mouseMoose": {
    "scareWithin": 6, "scaresToGiveUp": 5, "hideSeconds": 25, "creep": 1.2, "run": 5, "drag": 0.15, "dragAway": 0.5,
    "biteSeconds": 1.5, "grip": 0.7, "holeOut": 22, "atHole": 0.5, "reachEvery": 15, "leaveBeyond": 300,
    "tierWeights": { "local": 1, "frontier": 1.25, "deadLines": 1.5, "deepTerritory": 1.5 }
  },

  // THE HOUSE CREATURES (GDD §21; the director, 9 Oct 2026: "Every time I go into a house, it should feel like there could
  // be something lurking in there that wants to kill me, wants to chase me"; ARCHITECTURE §8 notes 583–586). Which of a
  // stop's open houses something lives in: "share" of them by tier, each house's own dice (the route's seed, the stop and the
  // building: nothing else's change), never the Gaunt's roost; what lives there by "weights" (a Householder only in a house
  // with something to find). Put in their houses, asleep, once the train's within placeWithin m of the stop, and gone once
  // it's forgetPast m past it. Not the director's: they cost it nothing ("enabled" off: none).
  // Note 719 (queue #453, the big finds): a stop's jackpot house (loot.json jackpotHouse), locked up with its better things,
  // rolls against its share times jackpotShare (never past 1): weighted, not certain.
  "dwellings": {
    "enabled": true,
    "share": { "local": 0.2, "frontier": 0.25, "deadLines": 0.33, "deepTerritory": 0.5 },
    "weights": { "lodger": 3, "householder": 2, "hollowHouse": 1.5, "hanger": 3 },
    "jackpotShare": 2,
    "placeWithin": 500, "forgetPast": 800,
    // A stop on the run in to the terminus (the line's terminus_safe stretch or route.json's final approach, where nothing
    // else new comes) has its houses' own only with inHomeStretch (note 912; note 887 found they always did). The director's
    // call (the inbox): false, the default taken, keeps the houses there empty.
    "inHomeStretch": false
  },
  // THE LODGER · sound · outside (note 583; docs/design/creatures/lodger.md). Folded in the house's darkest corner (the spot
  // furthest from its doors, hideInset m off the walls), breathing. Someone in its house noticeSeconds, or within
  // shriekWithin m of it, and it SHRIEKS for shriekSeconds (the telegraph: the spine's least, minReactionSeconds), then lunges at where they were, at lungeSpeed m/s
  // up to lungeReach m: within killWithin m of them and it has them (a grab of killWindow s: the one-hit kill, the director's
  // call). Missed, it chases (chase m/s) and shrieks again before every lunge; a shut door in its way it breaks open in
  // breakSeconds; anyone further than pursuitRadius m from its house's middle it gives up on, and walks back (walk m/s) to
  // its corner, resting there restSeconds. Only blows from behind as it walks back hurt it (health in blows).
  "lodger": {
    "hideInset": 0.6, "noticeSeconds": 2.5, "shriekWithin": 4.5, "shriekSeconds": 1.5,
    "lungeSpeed": 9, "lungeReach": 4.5, "killWithin": 0.9, "killWindow": 0.25,
    "chase": 5.0, "pursuitRadius": 25, "breakSeconds": 2, "walk": 1.6, "restSeconds": 3, "health": 4
  },
  // THE HOUSEHOLDER · sight · outside (note 584; docs/design/creatures/householder.md). Sat at its set table, watching whoever's
  // in its house; harmless to guests. Everything lying in its house is its own. Anything of yours left lying on its table
  // (within tableReach m of it) pays for one of its things. One of its things carried out of the house unpaid, it rises
  // (riseSeconds) and hunts whoever carries it at hunt m/s, to the train if it must: within grabReach m it has them (a grab of
  // grabSeconds a friend can break). Dropped, it takes the thing back home and sits again; carried off more than
  // giveUpBeyond m from its house, it gives up. Blows hurt it (health).
  "householder": {
    "tableReach": 1.0, "riseSeconds": 1.5, "hunt": 3.4, "grabReach": 1.0, "grabSeconds": 6, "giveUpBeyond": 200,
    "walk": 1.4, "health": 6
  },
  // THE HOLLOW HOUSE · vibration · outside (note 585; docs/design/creatures/hollow-house.md). The house is the creature.
  // Someone inside waitSeconds and the ground rumbles under it (the tell) for rumbleSeconds; then its doors slam shut one
  // every shutEvery s, held shut, and it sinks sinkDepth m over sinkSeconds and comes down on whoever's still inside (a crush
  // of "crush": a structure coming down kills, as a fall does). Then it stays as it fell. The answer is knowing the house.
  "hollowHouse": {
    "waitSeconds": 1.5, "rumbleSeconds": 3, "shutEvery": 0.35, "sinkSeconds": 3, "sinkDepth": 2.4, "crush": 1000
  },
  // THE HANGER · movement · outside (note 586; docs/design/creatures/hanger.md). In the roof space; "strands" strands hang
  // from the ceiling (2.6 m) to 0.9 m off the floor, spread over the house (Hanger.Strands). Walk into one (within
  // touchWithin m of it) and it has you (a grab of grabSeconds; a friend holding Use beside you, or a blow on it, frees you),
  // hauling you haulTo m up over haulSeconds (your feet off the floor, your head against the ceiling: a friend beside you can
  // still reach you). Freed, it draws back into the roof for retreatSeconds. Blows hurt it (health).
  "hanger": {
    "strands": 6, "touchWithin": 0.35, "haulSeconds": 2.5, "haulTo": 0.7, "grabSeconds": 10, "retreatSeconds": 25, "health": 3
  },
  // SOUND CUES IN THE WORLD (GDD §32 "Sound cues in the world", App. A.1; queue #466, ARCHITECTURE §8 note 732; the director,
  // 14 Oct 2026: "I do like the idea of using sound-only cues in the design of the environment"). For the living: heard where
  // they are, never on the HUD, each before what it tells of. Host-made, kept on the wire keepSeconds.
  // creak: boards taking a weight where a house creature waits (the Lodger in its corner, the Hanger in the roof), the first as
  // soon as anyone living is within `within` m (flat) of it (the Hanger: of one of its strands), then every everyFar s,
  // quickening to everyNear by `near` m: so a creak comes a few seconds before the Lodger's shriekWithin or a strand's touch.
  // The Householder shifts in its chair once as one of its things is lifted with nothing on its table to pay for it, and its
  // chair creaks the same way as the carrier nears its door (`within` of it), before it rises.
  // bell: a far bell (height m up, where a stop's bell would hang) where something of the crew's is lost out of their sight:
  // carsTaken, a car of theirs taken with nobody living within unseenBeyond m; cutsLost, a cut of theirs every living crewmate
  // is further from than run.json stranded.kitLostBeyond (§23.2: the night has it); holdoutsLeft, a Holdout released with a
  // friend still in it (App. D.5: the train gone on without them).
  // bark: a dog barking far off, `beyond` m out past a creature moving faster than movingAbove m/s between edgeFrom and edgeTo
  // m (flat) of the engine's rake and the living (the lamps' edge); not at the same creature for everyCreature s, nor at
  // anything for atMost s.
  "soundCues": {
    "enabled": true, "keepSeconds": 1,
    "creak": { "enabled": true, "within": 10, "near": 2, "everyFar": 2.4, "everyNear": 0.7 },
