  // The crew bots' answers to the six of 8 Oct (ARCHITECTURE §8 note 367; notes 362–367; not the creatures' own numbers, the
  // bots' judgement of them). A bot not driving goes to a body the Mourners are about within mournersWithin m of it, stands
  // over it and clubs them, chasing none further than mournersLeash m from it. On foot within towerJawWithin m of Tower Jaw
  // at its post it clubs it; gnawed past towerJawClearFrom it keeps crushRadius + towerJawClearBy m from where it falls. A
  // wreck across the line within wreckWithin m of a standing train is cleared (Use held at it); the driver stops
  // wreckStopShort m short of its near edge, braking hard from wreckHoldWithin m out. On foot within beetleWithin m of the
  // Freight Beetle it clubs it. Cornering the Brakeman, each of the pair closes to brakemanStandOff m off him on its side;
  // one with the other further off than brakeman.spook + 2 brakemanWaitPast m waits brakemanWaitPast m past his spook, and
  // cornered, one off his car within his cornerSpan less brakemanWaitPast keeps its place while the other is on it (note 610).
  // The driver stands for a seized axle or a wreck no longer than standGiveUp s.
  // Note 605 (queue #337; the director, 9 Oct: "plan a little extra time at the end of the run to stop the train, clear the
  // monsters, and then bring it in"): with something aboard a town's gate would charge for (note 589), within gateClearWithin
  // m of the gate the driver pulls up gateClearShort m short of it, in the quiet zone (note 590's spawnBanM), and stands while
  // the crew clears the train, no longer than gateClearGiveUp s, nor once the time in hand runs out: dawn, the Wakers' run up
  // to the train's rear (wakers.riseBehind at their speeds) where it isn't in past the gate (note 940: the walls the only safety),
  // less the run in and gateClearMargin s. No time, it runs straight in: a fee beats being eaten.
  // Note 615 (queue #347): from dawn, the driver stands for a Knotter, a Hotbox or its seized axle only while the Wakers' run
  // up to the train (note 607's reckoning) covers what's left of the stand, the run in through the gate at the night's cruise
  // and sixDawnMargin s; and waits for everyone aboard after only while it covers the run in. Short of that, it goes on.
  // Note 623: a body the Mourners are about is carried home into a car (up its side door's steps) when the foot of one's
  // within mournersCarryWithin m, and only while the dawn's time in hand covers mournersCarrySeconds and sixDawnMargin s and
  // the loading's not called done; else it's left (D1: "a body never costs the night"), and put down if it's in the arms.
  // Note 790: on foot within mouseMooseWithin m of the Mouse Moose at a casting (creeping in, its teeth in it, dragging it), it
  // goes at it and clubs it: it bolts long before (mouseMoose.scareWithin), and the casting's kept.
  // Note 894 (App. A.6, "outrunnable, if you run"): ribbitsOutnumberedRun, a bot on its way somewhere (aboard, say) with a pack
  // hunting it that outnumbers it and those with it runs on instead of turning to club them (frontier:6's shunter, alone at
  // the pick-up's points, went at a pack of three and was eaten).
  "crewBots": {
    "ribbitsOutnumberedRun": true,
    "mournersWithin": 30, "mournersLeash": 20, "towerJawWithin": 25, "towerJawClearFrom": 0.9, "towerJawClearBy": 2.5,
    "wreckWithin": 250, "wreckStopShort": 15, "wreckHoldWithin": 60, "beetleWithin": 15, "ribbitWithin": 12, "brakemanStandOff": 1.5,
    "brakemanWaitPast": 1, "standGiveUp": 240, "gateClearShort": 30, "gateClearWithin": 1500, "gateClearGiveUp": 240, "gateClearMargin": 45,
    "sixDawnMargin": 45, "mournersCarryWithin": 60, "mournersCarrySeconds": 60, "mouseMooseWithin": 30
  },

  // DAVE (GDD §3.2; the director, 8 Oct 2026: "a special NPC that shows up randomly in places ... If a player hits Dave 5
