  // THE WAKERS · what gets up at dawn (GDD §8; docs/design/creatures/wakers.md; note 588; the director, 9 Oct 2026: "The new
  // Dawn ending design is excellent ... The gargantuan creatures, the picking up of the train, especially with you in it").
  // enabled false is v1's dawn (the line goes live; the run fails run.json dawnGraceSeconds later). At dawn, count[tier] of
  // them rise (Local, Frontier, DeadLines, DeepTerritory): the first riseBehind m behind the train's rear on its path, the
  // rest riseAside m off either side and asideBack m further back, closing on the line over joinSeconds. Up after
  // riseSeconds, each runs startSpeed rising to topSpeed m/s over rampSeconds (faster than the engine's 22), over everything,
  // and, with the train home (its last car in through the terminus's gate), stops stopShort m short of the gate, under the
  // guns. Short of the gate the train is still theirs, however near the guns it stands (note 940; the director, 20 Oct 2026:
  // "unless I'm behind those walls fully, it should really make a good effort to try and get me"; stopShort was 300: "it
  // should stop maybe halfway"). The first one to come within catchShort m of the last car
  // has the train: it stops there, behind it, drags at dragFactor x the engine's pull, and from eatAfter s eats a car every
  // eatSeconds from the rear, whoever's in it with it. The engine eaten, the run's over: "taken at dawn". stirSeconds: the
  // tension before dawn (the sky, the ground, their calls; presentation and audio).
  // The lift (note 902; the director's playtest of 16 Oct 2026, line 29: "stop behind the train and like scoop it up with its
  // hands ... like a two-handed hot dog ... three bites per car"): a car at a time, in both hands. The last car goes up
  // from scoopFrom s into the hold till scoopHold s before eatAfter; each car after it in its own turn (its eatSeconds):
  // his hands down to it over reachShare of scoopShare of the turn, then up to his mouth over the rest of scoopShare. His
  // bites come at bites (fractions of the turn), the last as the turn ends and the sim has it eaten: three a car. Whoever's
  // down on the ground within fallAround m of the car in his hands, once it's fallFrom of the way up, fell from it.
  // Those who ran (note 710; the director, 14 Oct 2026: "It should capture players who escape the train and eat them too"):
  // while one holds the train, another rises out of the land pickAside m beyond each crewmate off it (up to pickers at once),
  // over pickRiseSeconds (the telegraph), strides to them at pickSpeed m/s, takes them within pickReach m, lifts them
  // over pickLiftSeconds to its mouth (pickMouthOut m in front of it, pickMouthHeight m up) and eats them; pickEatSeconds
  // after, it goes for the next. In under a fort's guns, nobody's taken.
  "wakers": { "enabled": true, "stirSeconds": 180, "count": [1, 1, 2, 3], "riseBehind": 1200, "riseAside": 600, "asideBack": 300,
    "joinSeconds": 90, "riseSeconds": 8, "startSpeed": 6, "topSpeed": 26, "rampSeconds": 45, "stopShort": 150,
    "dragFactor": 3, "eatAfter": 6, "eatSeconds": 4, "catchShort": 12, "scoopFrom": 1.2, "scoopHold": 1, "scoopShare": 0.45,
    "reachShare": 0.35, "bites": [0.55, 0.775], "fallFrom": 0.15, "fallAround": 3,
    // Note 940 (the director, 20 Oct 2026: "pick up the train while it's moving"): the train he has is brought to a stand in
    // his hands at holdDecel m/s² at the least (going or backing), dragFactor's pull or this, whichever's more. Shot, he's hit
    // (bodies.waker; stood, kneelStoop of it down on his knees), and nothing hurts him.
    "holdDecel": 6, "kneelStoop": 0.5,
    "pickers": 3, "pickAside": 40, "pickRiseSeconds": 4, "pickSpeed": 12, "pickReach": 18, "pickLiftSeconds": 4,
    "pickMouthOut": 10, "pickMouthHeight": 22, "pickEatSeconds": 4,
    // wakers.md §2, the night things run (note 635; the director, the inbox, 12 Oct 2026: "creatures should leave all except
    // the knotter and the hotbox who are parasites that have train functions"): nightFleesSeconds before dawn the night's
    // creatures let go and are gone, and the director sends none of them after; negative, they stay. Those staysAtDawn names
    // (as in the director's "costs") stay aboard through it. The director's Creature Tweaker sets each one's tick, and the
    // seconds (35, note 652).
    "nightFleesSeconds": 35, "staysAtDawn": ["knotter", "hotbox"] },

  // SOOT CHILDREN · sound · outside (App. A.6, B.6). Calling from callOut m every callEvery s. realChance of a real
  // survivor (a host's first-ever call is always real). A Soot Child lunges at anyone within lungeWithin m and drinks for
  // drainSeconds, gaining healthPerSecond blows a second while it does. Ignored for ignoredSeconds, it gives up. Alone, the
  // call comes too (the director, 15 Oct, note 770): it's the only way a solo night has a child in it.
