  // THE GAUNT · sound (silence) · outside (App. A.6, B.6). Asleep; stirs at stirAt m, wakes at wakeAt m and follows its
  // waker at followAt m. Every silenceSeconds with nobody talking (voice above talkingAbove, 0-255) within listenRadius,
  // its anger climbs one; at attackAt it attacks. Led into a car, it takes the most valuable thing there (or, with none,
  // lootCargo of the best load) and leaves: out through the car's nearest door and off into the dark at leaveSpeed (m/s,
  // "walking pace", App. A.6), in full view: clutched under its body by the hips, hanging carryHigh m up as it stalks
  // and carryLow as it creeps aboard (the sac's underside in each, tools/blender/gaunt.py); it's gone with it once it's
  // clearedAt m from the train. Kill it before then and it drops it.
  // anyVoiceCounts: whose voice holds it off (GDD Part Eleven Q9, open): anyone's (true) or only its waker's.
  // Note 272 (App. F.1, no chip damage): its blows are heavy hits, 60 every 4 s (were 35 every 2): two, then the crush.
  // minCrew (note 795, was 2): a crew of one meets it too; its waker's own voice holds it off, and a lone player can struggle
  // free of its crush (grab.soloStruggleChance).
  "gaunt": {
    "stirAt": 9, "wakeAt": 4, "followAt": 1.2, "followSpeed": 3, "listenRadius": 8, "silenceSeconds": 5, "talkingAbove": 40,
    "anyVoiceCounts": true, "attackAt": 4, "reach": 1.6, "hitDamage": 60, "hitEvery": 4, "grabBelowHealth": 35,
    "crushSeconds": 8, "health": 8, "lootCargo": 0.3, "lingerSeconds": 900, "minCrew": 1, "spawnOut": 25,
    "longStopWeight": 2, "longStopSeconds": 120, "leaveSpeed": 1.4, "clearedAt": 30, "carryHigh": 1.7,
    "carryLow": 0.55,
    // Note 945 (the director's playtest of 20 Oct evening, line 19: "I think I just saw a gaunt. Oh, but it just disappeared"):
    // leaving with what it took, it went the moment it was clearedAt m off the train, in the crew's lamps. Now it walks on until
    // no living crewmate out in the open (not in a car or the cab) is within goneUnseenAt m too (0: gone at clearedAt,
    // whoever's watching).
    "goneUnseenAt": 60,
    // Note 288 (drivenOff; "keep talking to it"). talkingCalms: talk brings its anger down a step every silenceSeconds (Part
    // Eleven Q9's "does talking lower its aggro", answered yes for now; false: talk only holds it); calmed under attackAt it
    // stops attacking; calm and talked to for talkedDownSeconds, it leaves empty-handed. Only the gang's blows with someone
