  // CAR FIRE (App. C.5, a supporting system: Fire Flies start it, as can a lamp dropped in a car). It grows; past
  // burnFrom it burns anyone within burnReach and the car's cargo and integrity; past spreadFrom for spreadSeconds it
  // takes the next car. Each car has a wall-mounted extinguisher: Fire held within sprayReach knocks it back
  // sprayPerSecond, for chargeSeconds of spray, recharging over rechargeSeconds on its bracket. DESIGN-TODO: the GDD has
  // no numbers; these let one crewmate who gets there in the half minute a fire takes to take hold put it out with one
  // extinguisher, and a fire left longer need two.
  // App. B.9 (note 182): coal and timber "burn" (§19) and "fire cascades escalate faster": a car of either grows fuelGrowth
  // times as fast and runs its spread clock fuelSpread times as fast. Gunpowder and shot "explodes" (§19): a powder car with
  // cargo left in it at explodeAt (full blaze) goes up once, the car and its cargo gone; everyone within explodeKillRadius m
  // takes explodeDamage (killed), less with distance out to explodeRadius; the cars either side catch. DESIGN-TODO: not in
  // the GDD's numbers: the kill radius is the powder car's own length and its neighbours' near ends.
  "carFire": {
    "startIntensity": 0.1, "growPerSecond": 0.006, "growWithSize": 0.02, "burnFrom": 0.35,
    // sprayReach 4.5 (note 939; the director's playtest of 20 Oct evening, line 10: "The fire extinguisher is working.
    // Admittedly, though, I feel like I have to walk a little too close to them"): it was 3.5, inside the fire's 1.6 m burn
    // of a 3.5 m cell's patch; now a stretch can be sprayed from the stretch before it, out of its burn.
    "sprayReach": 4.5,
    // sprayPerSecond: the director, the inbox, 12 Oct (`D1.4-burning-car-beatable`, "b": "make it 15 and have the extinguisher
    // extinguish far more of the fire. A car should be extinguished from full blaze within 20 seconds."; note 634): 2, twice
    // what it was, and with 16 cells (cellSize below) one extinguisher has a car at full blaze out in about 10.5 s (FireCellsTests).
    // Note 662 (the director, 13 Oct, playing: "I'm not getting visual feedback that the fire is going out ... I should be able
    // to point at it ... one grid ahead of me. I should be able to hold. And it should dissipate within five seconds. And then
    // I should be able to continue walking forward to the next grid"): sprayWorksAcross, the spray works all round the car
    // where it's aimed (its floor, walls and roof there, a 3.5 m stretch of it), each of those cells at sprayPerSecond. At
    // 1 the stretch dies from full blaze to out in about a second, its flames shrinking as it goes (the director's "1s per
    // grid" of 8 Oct, note 467, a grid now all round the car), and stays out while it's wet (dampSeconds); one cell aimed at
    // on the floor alone went out under walls and a roof still burning over it.
    "sprayWorksAcross": true,
    "sprayPerSecond": 1.0, "chargeSeconds": 15, "rechargeSeconds": 90, "burnReach": 1.6,
    // Note 587 (the director, 9 Oct 2026, playtesting: "I point at fire, I click, I hold, it should stay there"): the spray
    // goes where the look lands on fire; where it lands on none (looking at the flames over a burning cell, the ray goes on
    // to the boards beyond), on the burning cell whose flames are nearest the middle of a sprayConeDeg cone along the look,
    // within sprayReach: its flames as tall as they're drawn, sprayAimLift + sprayAimLiftPerHeat x its heat (m) off its
    // surface. With none burning in it, on what the look hits.
    "sprayConeDeg": 25, "sprayAimLift": 0.4, "sprayAimLiftPerHeat": 1.2,
    // App. C.5: it burns "whoever's in it", and says no more. The director's decision of 6 Oct 2026 (note 263: "if I stay in
    // the fire too long, then yeah, I die, but I just barely touched it"): it burns by the second, not in lumps. Within
    // burnReach of it you take burnPerSecond x its intensity, at burnBrushShare of that the moment you're in it, rising to the
    // whole over burnRampSeconds; step out and it starts again from a brush. At full blaze a second in it is about 6 health,
    // and standing in it kills in about 11 s.
    "burnPerSecond": 10, "burnBrushShare": 0.5, "burnRampSeconds": 3,
    "cargoPerSecond": 0.003, "integrityPerSecond": 0.0015, "spreadFrom": 0.8, "spreadSeconds": 15,
    "chemicalSpread": 2, "chemicalGrowth": 1.3, "powderGrowth": 1.6, "fuelGrowth": 1.4, "fuelSpread": 2,
    "explodeAt": 0.6, "explodeRadius": 14, "explodeKillRadius": 5, "explodeDamage": 150,
    "burnOutPerSecond": 0.05, "maxActive": 3,
    // The director's decision of 6 Oct 2026 (App. F.1, note 267): "Fire is a grid". Each car's floor, walls and roof are cut
    // into cells of cellSize m; each has its own heat, 0..1. A cell starts at startIntensity, grows at growPerSecond +
    // growWithSize x its heat (the floor's cells x the cargo's growth: it's the cargo that's burning there), and burns up
    // charPerSecond x its heat of itself, charring; burnt out, it dies down at burnOutPerSecond. A cell at catchFrom or more
    // heats each cell sharing an edge with it at catchPerSecond x its heat, climb x that upward (up the walls, onto the roof).
    // The extinguisher (sprayReach from the eye, along the look) cools the cell it's aimed at by sprayPerSecond (1: a cell at
    // full blaze is out after a second of it, the director, 8 Oct 2026: "should be 1s per grid to put out"; note 467; it was
    // 0.35, three seconds and more a cell, and holding it on a fire didn't feel like it did anything), and the cells
    // round it by sprayShare of that, and wets it for dampSeconds: it won't catch again from round it until it dries. It's
    // alight (the commit) when a cell's at burnFrom; the car's fire, for the explosion, damage and the sound, is the mean of
    // its cells (explodeAt: more than half the powder car well alight). It jumps the coupling from a cell against an end
    // wall at spreadFrom for spreadSeconds. It burns whoever's within burnReach m of a burning cell's patch (half a cell
    // round its centre; from their feet to bodyHeight up), by that cell's heat less with distance, the roof's at
    // ceilingBurnShare. A cell below outBelow is embers: it doesn't grow on its own, and goes out unless a cell round it
    // is heating it (a sprayed cell doesn't creep back from a spark). DESIGN-TODO: the GDD has no numbers; these keep
    // one crewmate who gets to a fire in its first half minute able to put it out with one extinguisher, a fire left a
    // minute needing two, and a car left alone taking the next in about a minute and a half.
    // cellSize 3.5 (the director, 12 Oct, "72 patches of fire per car is far too many, make it 15"; note 634): 16 cells in a
    // cargo car (4 along, the floor, the roof and each wall one across), the nearest the grid comes to 15; it was 1.5, 72.
    // burnPatch: the boards round a burning cell's centre that burn you as if you stood on them, the reach counted from there
    // (note 634): 0.75, half the 1.5 m cells it was tuned on, so the bigger cells don't burn further.
    "burnPatch": 0.75,
    // doorwayClear (note 939; the director's playtest of 20 Oct evening, line 12: "I get burned when I'm getting into a car"
    // to fight a fire): stood in one of the car's open doorways, within this of its opening (m), the fire doesn't burn you;
    // it's the fire's edge, where the crew board to fight it. A side door's walls either side are burning cells at 3.5 m,
    // and their reach took in the whole doorway. 0: burnt in the doorway as anywhere inside.
    "doorwayClear": 0.8,
    "cellSize": 3.5, "catchFrom": 0.5, "catchPerSecond": 0.04, "climb": 2, "charPerSecond": 0.01,
    "sprayShare": 0.4, "dampSeconds": 3, "ceilingBurnShare": 0.5, "bodyHeight": 1.8, "outBelow": 0.05
  },

  "choirSwarm": {
    // Legacy (T9): the Choir's damage to the exposed is now its ghosts' seize (above); kept for old saves' tuning.
